WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.176
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:16.830
Unit sixteen: Numbers & Quantities (some/any). Today you will talk about amounts with some, any, how many and how much.

4
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.875
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.997
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.677
Some.

7
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:29.565
Some means an amount in positive sentences.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.604
I have some apples.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:34.138
Your turn. Say: Some.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.792
Some.

11
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.342
Any.

12
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.011
Any means an amount in questions and negatives.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:44.908
Do you have any water?

14
00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:47.461
Your turn. Say: Any.

15
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:50.988
Any.

16
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.739
How many.

17
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.295
How many means a question about countable things.

18
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:58.651
How many books do you have?

19
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.937
Your turn. Say: How many.

20
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.871
How many.

21
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.420
How much.

22
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:11.566
How much means a question about uncountable things or price.

23
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.488
How much water do you need?

24
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.678
Your turn. Say: How much.

25
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:20.453
How much.

26
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:22.102
A few.

27
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:25.790
A few means a small number of countable things.

28
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:27.849
I have a few friends.

29
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.009
Your turn. Say: A few.

30
00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:34.926
A few.

31
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:36.499
A little.

32
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:40.296
A little means a small amount of uncountable things.

33
00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:42.418
I need a little water.

34
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:45.054
Your turn. Say: A little.

35
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:48.889
A little.

36
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.581
Quantity.

37
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:54.129
Quantity means the amount or number of something.

38
00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:56.112
What is the quantity?

39
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:58.951
Your turn. Say: Quantity.

40
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.708
Quantity.

41
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.312
Countable.

42
00:02:05.317 --> 00:02:07.618
Countable means something you can count.

43
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.659
Apples are countable.

44
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.508
Your turn. Say: Countable.

45
00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.275
Countable.

46
00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:20.578
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.417 --> 00:02:25.613
Visal, in a shop you say 'I want some rice.' Why some?

48
00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:38.009
We use some in positive sentences for an unknown amount: I have some apples. We use any in questions and negatives: Do you have any water? I don't have any money.

49
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.756
And how many and how much?

50
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:52.156
How many is for countable nouns: How many books? How much is for uncountable nouns: How much water? Also how much asks about price.

51
00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.948
What about small amounts?

52
00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:08.063
Use a few with countable nouns: a few friends. Use a little with uncountable nouns: a little water. They both show a small, but useful, quantity.

53
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.863
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.717 --> 00:03:16.340
Grammar focus: Quantities: some and any and a few and a little.

55
00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.850
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.981
I have some apples.

57
00:03:20.883 --> 00:03:22.244
Do you have any water?

58
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.615
I need a little time.

59
00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:36.836
Use some in positive sentences and any in questions and negatives. Use how many with countable nouns and how much with uncountable nouns. A few is countable; a little is uncountable.

60
00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.514
Be careful! Don't say: I don't have some money.

61
00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:44.420
Say: I don't have any money.

62
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.568
Use any in negatives.

63
00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.356
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.319
At the Market.

65
00:03:52.619 --> 00:03:54.618
I need some rice and some eggs.

66
00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:58.553
Do you have any milk? No, I don't have any.

67
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.567
How many eggs do you want? A few, please.

68
00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:06.347
How much rice do you need? Only a little.

69
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.983
Countable things are things we can count, like eggs.

70
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:15.161
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.017 --> 00:04:18.039
I have blank friends in this class.

72
00:04:18.339 --> 00:04:21.296
A, some. B, any. C, much.

73
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:26.473
The answer is A: some.

74
00:04:27.617 --> 00:04:29.071
Do you have blank water?

75
00:04:29.371 --> 00:04:32.258
A, some. B, any. C, a few.

76
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.300
The answer is B: any.

77
00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.136
How blank rice do you want?

78
00:04:40.436 --> 00:04:43.428
A, many. B, much. C, few.

79
00:04:46.967 --> 00:04:48.862
The answer is B: much.

80
00:04:50.017 --> 00:04:51.645
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:51.945 --> 00:04:56.620
A, I don't have some money.. B, I don't have any money.. C, I have any money..

82
00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.770
The answer is B: I don't have any money..

83
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:06.473
According to the reading, what do they need a little of?

84
00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:09.916
A, rice. B, eggs. C, friends.

85
00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:15.420
The answer is A: rice.

86
00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:19.959
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.817 --> 00:05:23.408
Write one sentence with 'some' and one with 'any'.

88
00:05:32.217 --> 00:05:33.694
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:33.994 --> 00:05:47.890
I have some books in my bag. I don't have any pens today. I use some in a positive sentence and any in a negative sentence. In a question, I also use any: Do you have any pens?

90
00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.818
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:56.330
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and quantities: some and any and a few and a little.

92
00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:01.348
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:01.648 --> 00:06:04.498
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.798 --> 00:06:07.613
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

